# VAZEDGAME — Environment Variables
# Supabase authentication setup required.
# 1. Create a Supabase project at https://supabase.io
# 2. Go to Project Settings → API
# 3. Copy the values below

# SUPABASE_URL: Your Supabase project URL (server-side, in Vercel Functions)
#   Example: https://xyzcompany.supabase.co
SUPABASE_URL=

# SUPABASE_ANON_KEY: Your Supabase publishable/anon key (server-side for Functions,
#   also usable in frontend with proper RLS policies)
#   Example: eyJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiIsInR5cCI6IkpXVCJ9...
SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=

# NOTE: SESSION_SECRET is not required — Supabase manages session tokens
# securely via its own authentication mechanism (access_token + refresh_token cookies).
# Do not add this variable unless you have a custom need (not required for current architecture).

# For the frontend (plain HTML), these same SUPABASE_URL and SUPABASE_ANON_KEY values
# must be made available. In Vercel, add them as environment variables and they will
# be accessible to server-side functions via process.env.SUPABASE_URL and
# process.env.SUPABASE_ANON_KEY.

# VITE_ prefixed variables require a build step (Vite, Create React App, etc.)
# This project uses plain HTML + Vercel Functions, so VITE_ variables are NOT
# automatically available in browser code. Use SUPABASE_URL and SUPABASE_ANON_KEY instead.

# Optional: For custom use (not required for current setup)
# SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=your_service_role_key_here  # NEVER expose to browser